{"title":"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> are isosceles with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/9290d0dfc81b1c5b202d036f1475cb7994f5a6f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AC=BD$\" width=\"134\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/b/37b3e34752e20a8e619fd672480528e1d9972cca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle C+\\angle D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74dbdbc2ea44c18c583ca2b60609b48b4fbc1fd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(120); pair B=origin, A=1*dir(70), M=foot(A, B, (3,0)), C=reflect(A, M)*B, E=foot(B, A, C), D=1*dir(20); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^E); draw(A--D--B--A--C--B); markscalefactor=0.005; draw(rightanglemark(A, E, B)); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^E); pair point=midpoint(A--M); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, dir(point--A)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, dir(point--B)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, dir(point--C)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, dir(point--D)); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, dir(point--E)); [/asy]\" width=\"202\" height=\"198\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/4/0d40f7b39b79d5fb4c3a46e5644f69165e1744b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 115^\\circ\\qquad\\text{(B)}\\ 120^\\circ\\qquad\\text{(C)}\\ 130^\\circ\\qquad\\text{(D)}\\ 135^\\circ\\qquad\\text{(E)}\\ \\text{not uniquely determined}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"602\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Redraw the figure as a concave pentagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/0/98030cde061e34a3e61c33a473b9033b353b7a81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADECB$\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/1/9c118f5f6e65f9b66fe4ba544081f736247500d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(120); pair B=origin, A=1*dir(70), M=foot(A, B, (3,0)), C=reflect(A, M)*B, E=foot(B, A, C), D=1*dir(20); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^E); draw(A--D--E--C--B--A); markscalefactor=0.005; draw(rightanglemark(D, E, C)); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^E); pair point=midpoint(A--M); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, dir(point--A)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, dir(point--B)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, dir(point--C)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, dir(point--D)); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, dir(point--E)); [/asy]\" width=\"202\" height=\"198\" />\n</p><p>The angles of the pentagon will still sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/9162408ab730c795387e564416b0990a56a458b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ \\cdot 3 = 540^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"114\" height=\"13\" />, regardless of whether the pentagon is concave or not.  As a quick proof, note that the nine angles of three original triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/b/a1b3b8188354494cb248bd9965a24d0b9f1ef814.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle  AEB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f6e39d5f7fb024a2c1e7ff1f03309c49722ed8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CBE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/9/a79ef38acd8198300ef945366a4c5d7b360f808b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> all make up the angles of the pentagon without overlap.\n</p><p>Since reflex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/d/bfd3f1bef7cbbe6ae34362b57deebc730ed46725.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle E = 270^\\circ$\" width=\"84\" height=\"13\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cf0a054d2a3df015eb69e5024266f0a8d27d4c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle C + \\angle B + \\angle A + \\angle D = 540^\\circ - 270^\\circ = 270^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"349\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>From isosceles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb93eba5ed285b1b9fc5d644d0442fa97e7afb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B = \\angle C$\" width=\"79\" height=\"12\" />, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de8eaf82a64a6031cc0291dfb634efee429ce060.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\angle C + \\angle D + \\angle A = 270^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"193\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>From isosceles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02f6862c019809ba2e2e7e7957e3919a6339b21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A = \\angle D$\" width=\"78\" height=\"13\" />, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/8/c7839c0311f70d2cd6fb1abd3a4cafaadb85f176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\angle C + 2\\angle D = 270^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"153\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/09421c51bc5c4ed69afe2da570ac07c845d09de2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle C + \\angle D = 135^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"135\" height=\"14\" />, which is answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/9/469596e9bd2e8ac681e70efe46979033fdfb7b34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ABC = x$\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" />. By the isosceles triangle theorem, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcf6b8fd8c4c75acea09003659a42bc019b626d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ACB = x$\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/4/eb413d1f9eaefb933855ccae155220187669695d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle BAD = m\\angle BDA$\" width=\"169\" height=\"13\" />. Because the angles of a triangle sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/e/36ef6568585d45e2504d028967bb88f0f5c2bc05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle BAC = \\pi - 2x$\" width=\"148\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/2/b3202f31e5c4f452efd95b02f06b8a47aef70b61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ABD=\\frac{\\pi}{2}-(\\pi-2x)=2x-\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"280\" height=\"33\" />. Then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/c/89c15f2405f898604c9cd2cf9558b747817fde4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle BAD + m\\angle BDA = \\pi - m\\angle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"297\" height=\"14\" />. Substituting, this becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0a60de15075ad03297ca778031233ae48508999.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2m\\angle BDA = \\pi-\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-(\\pi-2x)\\right) \\to m \\angle BDA = \\frac{3 \\pi}{4} - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"446\" height=\"38\" />. Adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/274420680951b694c5a6c39f72197434da5846a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ACB$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31bd61cd97b5017c4f3c7804e361fc12c44f619c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle BDA + m\\angle ACB = \\frac{3 \\pi}{4} = 135^\\circ \\to \\boxed{\\textbf{D}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"328\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME\" title=\"1996 AHSME\">1996 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1996 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1996\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017185544\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 261/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2494/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 152/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7976/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.